.TH GUGA 1 "2026" "guga 1.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
guga \- send notifications to Android via the GuGa server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B guga
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIMESSAGE\fR | \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.br
.B echo
\fI"message"\fR |
.B guga
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B guga
is a command-line notification tool that sends messages to an Android device
via a local GuGa ASGI server. It supports three primary modes:
.PP
.B Message mode
sends a plain string as a push notification.
.PP
.B Run mode
executes a command, streams its output to the terminal as normal, then
sends a notification with the exit status, elapsed time, and last line of output.
.PP
.B Interactive mode
allows remote interaction with the command-line via a paired device,
forwarding terminal prompts and receiving replies in real-time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-message
Force message mode. All positional arguments are joined into a single string.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-run
Force run mode. Positional arguments are treated as a command to execute.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Enable remote interaction (PTY wrapping) for \fBrun mode\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-ask\-user \fIPROMPT\fR
Synchronous request-reply loop. Sends \fIPROMPT\fR to a device and waits for a reply.
.TP
.B \-\-send\-to \fIDEVICE_ID\fR
Target a specific device or custom tag (e.g. \fB--send-to F\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-delay \fIDURATION\fR
Timeout for \fB--ask-user\fR replies (e.g. \fB120s\fR, \fB5m\fR, \fBnever\fR). Default: never.
.TP
.B \-\-default \fIVALUE\fR
Fallback value returned by \fB--ask-user\fR when the timeout expires (exit code 0).
.TP
.B \-\-look\-for \fIREGEX\fR
In run mode, send an immediate notification whenever this regex matches a line of output.
.TP
.B \-\-expect \fIREGEX\fR
Custom regex for prompt detection in interactive mode. Default: \fB[:?>]\\s*$\fR
.TP
.B \-t, \-f, \-\-from, \-\-title \fILABEL\fR
Set the notification title / sender label (e.g. \fB"GPU Server"\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-status
Show the current service status and connected devices.
.TP
.B \-\-qr
Show the pairing QR code and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-url
Print the raw pairing URL (scriptable; no QR).
.TP
.B \-\-approve [\-A / \-\-all]
Interactively approve pending pairing requests. \fB-A\fR approves all without prompting.
.TP
.B \-\-rename\-device
Assign a custom short tag to a connected device.
.TP
.B \-\-blocked
List all devices currently on the blocklist.
.TP
.B \-\-unblock [\fIDEVICE_ID\fR]
Remove a device from the blocklist. Omit ID for interactive selection.
.TP
.B \-\-revoke [\fIDEVICE_ID\fR]
Revoke trust for a previously paired device. Omit ID for interactive selection.
.TP
.B \-\-start\-server [\-b / \-\-background] [\-\-mode lan|public]
Start the GuGa ASGI server. Use \fB-b\fR for a detached background process.
\fB--mode public\fR enables internet access via Cloudflare Tunnel.
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-server [\-A / \-\-all]
Stop background GuGa server(s). \fB-A\fR stops all without prompting.
.TP
.B \-\-reload\-server
Restart the background GuGa service.
.TP
.B \-\-mcp
Start the MCP server in stdio mode (for local AI tools such as Antigravity or Claude Desktop).
.TP
.B \-\-mcp\-token
Generate a JWT access token for remote MCP access via Cloudflare Tunnel.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-mcp [\-\-mcp\-python \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-dry\-run]
Write the GuGa stdio MCP server entry into the Antigravity config
\fI~/.gemini/antigravity/mcp_config.json\fR. Auto-detects the correct Python
interpreter (prefers active venv, then sibling venvs, then system python).
Use \fB--mcp-python\fR to specify an interpreter explicitly.
Use \fB--dry-run\fR to preview changes without writing any files.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall\-mcp [\-\-dry\-run]
Remove the 'guga' entry from the Antigravity MCP config. \fB--dry-run\fR previews.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-service [\-\-reconfigure]
Install GuGa as a systemd background service. \fB--reconfigure\fR re-runs the
interactive setup even if already installed.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-skills
Copy the GuGa AI skill (SKILL.md, llms.txt, tools.json) to \fI.agents/skills/guga/\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
Remove all GuGa system components (service, man page, config directory).
.TP
.B \-\-choices \fIVALUES\fR
Pre-fill interactive prompts with comma-separated values (e.g. \fB"1,2,,y"\fR).
Empty tokens (\fB,,\fR) accept the default. Useful for non-interactive automation.
.TP
.B \-\-silent
Suppress guga's own console output.
.TP
.B \-\-server \fIPORT\fR
Override the GuGa server port (default: 6769).
.TP
.B \-A, \-\-all
Apply current action to ALL items without asking (used with \fB--approve\fR, \fB--stop-server\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the current version (1.5.1) and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Message mode
.B guga "Build finished \[u2705]"
.PP
.B echo "Deploy done" | guga --send-to F
.SS Run mode
.B guga python train.py
.PP
.B guga -r --look-for "ERROR|CRITICAL" ./long_script.sh
.SS Interactive mode
.B guga -r -i --send-to F ./deploy.sh
(Forwards terminal prompts to device F in real-time)
.SS Ask user
.B guga --ask-user "Deploy to production?" --send-to F --delay 10m --default no
.SS MCP installation (one-time setup)
.B guga --install-mcp
.PP
(Writes the guga entry to ~/.gemini/antigravity/mcp_config.json with the correct Python interpreter)
.PP
.B guga --install-mcp --dry-run
.PP
(Preview without writing)
.PP
.B guga --uninstall-mcp
.PP
(Remove the guga entry from the MCP config)
.SS Device management
.B guga --blocked
.PP
.B guga --unblock android-a3f9...
.PP
.B guga --revoke F
.SH SERVER
The server is powered by an asynchronous ASGI architecture (\fBQuart\fR / \fBUvicorn\fR),
providing non-blocking concurrency for multiple simultaneous interactive sessions.
.PP
The MCP server runs in stdio mode and communicates with local AI tools via
standard input/output. It wraps the HTTP API exposed by the running GuGa server.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits with the same code as the watched command in run mode, or 0 on success in
message / ask-user mode. Non-zero exit from \fB--ask-user\fR indicates a timeout
(unless \fB--default\fR was provided).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.guga/.env
Runtime configuration (PORT, MODE, ENABLE_OS_NOTIFICATIONS, etc.)
.TP
.I ~/.guga/logs/
Per-invocation output logs (filename = unique message ID).
.TP
.I ~/.gemini/antigravity/mcp_config.json
Antigravity MCP server configuration. Managed by \fB--install-mcp\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/guga/config
Persistent CLI defaults (title, port, silent).
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the GuGa project contributors.
